        "original_id": "44b822b9-d6db-506d-a055-3797c37261c1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Memphis International Airport, Southwest Georgia Regional Airport, Logan International Airport, Memphis, Albany, Shelby County, Dougherty County, Tennessee, Georgia, New York, Boston, Massachusetts, United States\n- Organizations: FedEx Express\n- Events: FedEx Express Flight 1406\n- Concepts: airport identifiers, civil-military airport, public-use airport, cargo flight, cargo fire\n\nFacts:\n- Memphis International Airport is a civil-military airport located seven miles southeast of downtown Memphis in Shelby County, Tennessee, United States.\n- Memphis International Airport has the airport identifiers IATA MEM, ICAO KMEM, and FAA LID MEM.\n- Southwest Georgia Regional Airport is a city-owned, public-use airport located three nautical miles southwest of the central business district of Albany in Dougherty County, Georgia, United States.\n- Southwest Georgia Regional Airport has the airport identifiers IATA ABY, ICAO KABY, and FAA LID ABY.\n- FedEx Express Flight 1406 was a cargo flight from Memphis International Airport in Memphis, Tennessee, to Logan International Airport in Boston, Massachusetts.\n- FedEx Express Flight 1406 suffered an in-flight cargo fire over New York.",
